<h1>connected graph</h1>
<p>
(definition)
</p>

<p>
<strong>Definition:</strong>
An <a href="undirectedGraph.html"><em>undirected graph</em></a> that has a <a href="path.html"><em>path</em></a> between every pair of <a href="vertex.html"><em>vertices</em></a>.
</p>

<p>
<strong>See also</strong>
<a href="completeGraph.html"><em>complete graph</em></a>, <a href="biconnectedGraph.html"><em>biconnected graph</em></a>, <a href="triconnectedGraph.html"><em>triconnected graph</em></a>, <a href="stronglyConnectedGraph.html"><em>strongly connected graph</em></a>, <a href="forest.html"><em>forest</em></a>, <a href="bridge.html"><em>bridge</em></a>, <a href="reachable.html"><em>reachable</em></a>, <a href="maximallyConnectedComponent.html"><em>maximally connected component</em></a>, <a href="connectedComponents.html"><em>connected components</em></a>, <a href="vertexConnectivity.html"><em>vertex connectivity</em></a>, <a href="edgeConnectivity.html"><em>edge connectivity</em></a>.
</p>

<p>
<em>Note:
After LK.</em>
</p>

<p>Author: <a href="../Other/contrib.html#authorPEB">PEB</a></p>

